**`src/lib.rs:35-39`** — new `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Exact-match via `==` (not substring), preserves relative order (single `filter` pass over `notes`).

**`src/main.rs`** — `list` command now parses `--tag <TAG>` from the remaining args. When present, output goes through `filter_by_tag`; otherwise all notes print as before. Missing `--tag` value errors out.

